      "audioScript": "Alex: Hi Minh! What futuristic technology or green project are you presenting today?\nMinh: Hi Alex! I am presenting about Upcycling Used Plastic Bottles into Creative Planters and its application in art workshop.\nAlex: How will it help our society or environment?\nMinh: It utilizes recycled plastic jugs and enables humans to practice growing balcony flowers.\nAlex: Does it also improve painting colourful designs?\nMinh: Yes, and it significantly enhances sustainability by incorporating school craft exhibition.\nAlex: Fantastic! That will help our planet become much greener and smarter.",
      "clozeText": "Technological innovation and green living are shaping our future. In the coming decades, people in art workshop will rely on recycled plastic jugs to power their daily routines. If we actively practice (23) ________ and energy conservation, our cities will become cleaner. Many experts predict that helper robots (24) ________ take over dangerous household and industrial tasks. However, citizens (25) ________ depend entirely on machines for basic personal responsibilities. Furthermore, integrating school craft exhibition proves that human ingenuity can protect the natural (26) ________. In conclusion, living in harmony with smart technology will foster a (27) ________ society.",
      "readingText": "Upcycling Used Plastic Bottles into Creative Planters represents an inspiring milestone in the transition toward a cleaner and more technologically advanced world. Situated within art workshop, this initiative demonstrates how recycled plastic jugs and painting colourful designs can reduce carbon footprints effectively. Families and students who adopt growing balcony flowers report remarkable decreases in electricity costs and municipal waste generation. In addition, engineers have embedded school craft exhibition to maximize renewable efficiency and ensure long-term reliability. Environmentalists emphasize that individual actions, such as sorting rubbish and turning off idle gadgets, complement high-tech automation. By combining responsible environmental ethics with intelligent robotic systems, humankind can build a prosperous, sustainable future.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nTechnological innovation and green living are shaping our future. In the coming decades, people in art workshop will rely on recycled plastic jugs to power their daily routines. If we actively practice (23) ________ and energy conservation, our cities will become cleaner. Many experts predict that helper robots (24) ________ take over dangerous household and industrial tasks. However, citizens (25) ________ depend entirely on machines for basic personal responsibilities. Furthermore, integrating school craft exhibition proves that human ingenuity can protect the natural (26) ________. In conclusion, living in harmony with smart technology will foster a (27) ________ society.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nUpcycling Used Plastic Bottles into Creative Planters represents an inspiring milestone in the transition toward a cleaner and more technologically advanced world. Situated within art workshop, this initiative demonstrates how recycled plastic jugs and painting colourful designs can reduce carbon footprints effectively. Families and students who adopt growing balcony flowers report remarkable decreases in electricity costs and municipal waste generation. In addition, engineers have embedded school craft exhibition to maximize renewable efficiency and ensure long-term reliability. Environmentalists emphasize that individual actions, such as sorting rubbish and turning off idle gadgets, complement high-tech automation. By combining responsible environmental ethics with intelligent robotic systems, humankind can build a prosperous, sustainable future.",
