      "audioScript": "Alex: Hi Minh! What futuristic technology or green project are you presenting today?\nMinh: Hi Alex! I am presenting about Zero-Energy Underground Homes with Geothermal Cooling and its application in underground eco-dwelling.\nAlex: How will it help our society or environment?\nMinh: It utilizes geothermal ventilation tubes and enables humans to practice keeping constant temperature.\nAlex: Does it also improve natural sunlight skylights?\nMinh: Yes, and it significantly enhances sustainability by incorporating recycled brick walls.\nAlex: Fantastic! That will help our planet become much greener and smarter.",
      "clozeText": "Technological innovation and green living are shaping our future. In the coming decades, people in underground eco-dwelling will rely on geothermal ventilation tubes to power their daily routines. If we actively practice (23) ________ and energy conservation, our cities will become cleaner. Many experts predict that helper robots (24) ________ take over dangerous household and industrial tasks. However, citizens (25) ________ depend entirely on machines for basic personal responsibilities. Furthermore, integrating recycled brick walls proves that human ingenuity can protect the natural (26) ________. In conclusion, living in harmony with smart technology will foster a (27) ________ society.",
      "readingText": "Zero-Energy Underground Homes with Geothermal Cooling represents an inspiring milestone in the transition toward a cleaner and more technologically advanced world. Situated within underground eco-dwelling, this initiative demonstrates how geothermal ventilation tubes and natural sunlight skylights can reduce carbon footprints effectively. Families and students who adopt keeping constant temperature report remarkable decreases in electricity costs and municipal waste generation. In addition, engineers have embedded recycled brick walls to maximize renewable efficiency and ensure long-term reliability. Environmentalists emphasize that individual actions, such as sorting rubbish and turning off idle gadgets, complement high-tech automation. By combining responsible environmental ethics with intelligent robotic systems, humankind can build a prosperous, sustainable future.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nTechnological innovation and green living are shaping our future. In the coming decades, people in underground eco-dwelling will rely on geothermal ventilation tubes to power their daily routines. If we actively practice (23) ________ and energy conservation, our cities will become cleaner. Many experts predict that helper robots (24) ________ take over dangerous household and industrial tasks. However, citizens (25) ________ depend entirely on machines for basic personal responsibilities. Furthermore, integrating recycled brick walls proves that human ingenuity can protect the natural (26) ________. In conclusion, living in harmony with smart technology will foster a (27) ________ society.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nZero-Energy Underground Homes with Geothermal Cooling represents an inspiring milestone in the transition toward a cleaner and more technologically advanced world. Situated within underground eco-dwelling, this initiative demonstrates how geothermal ventilation tubes and natural sunlight skylights can reduce carbon footprints effectively. Families and students who adopt keeping constant temperature report remarkable decreases in electricity costs and municipal waste generation. In addition, engineers have embedded recycled brick walls to maximize renewable efficiency and ensure long-term reliability. Environmentalists emphasize that individual actions, such as sorting rubbish and turning off idle gadgets, complement high-tech automation. By combining responsible environmental ethics with intelligent robotic systems, humankind can build a prosperous, sustainable future.",
