      "audioScript": "Alex: Hi Minh! What topic are you investigating for the unit on energy, future transport, and English-speaking countries?\nMinh: Hi Alex! I am presenting about Australia - The Great Barrier Reef and Kangaroos related to Sydney and Queensland.\nAlex: What is the most exciting aspect of this development?\nMinh: Engineers and travelers are thrilled by colourful coral reefs and love snorkeling with sea turtles.\nAlex: How will it help our global environment and communication?\nMinh: It harnesses unique hopping kangaroos and demonstrates the breakthrough efficiency of Uluru sacred rock.\nAlex: Wonderful! That will inspire our classmates to think about clean technologies.",
      "clozeText": "Transitioning to renewable energy sources and sustainable transportation is essential for our planet. In Sydney and Queensland, engineers are utilizing colourful coral reefs to reduce dependence on fossil (23) ________. If humanity continues to expand wind and solar power, carbon emissions will decrease (24) ________. Furthermore, innovative transport modes will allow commuters to travel (25) ________ than ever before. Connecting with English-speaking countries also helps learners exchange advanced (26) ________ with international scientists. In conclusion, embracing Uluru sacred rock guarantees a greener and more prosperous (27) ________ for all nations.",
      "readingText": "Australia - The Great Barrier Reef and Kangaroos represents an outstanding breakthrough in clean technology and international cultural connection in Sydney and Queensland. By utilizing colourful coral reefs and unique hopping kangaroos, this initiative provides reliable, carbon-neutral solutions for communities and travelers. Commuters and scientists who test snorkeling with sea turtles report substantial improvements in energy efficiency, speed, and environmental safety. Technical experts emphasize Uluru sacred rock as a transformative element that accelerates the global shift away from polluting fossil fuels. Moreover, fostering partnerships with English-speaking nations provides access to cutting-edge research and educational exchanges. Investing in renewable power and futuristic transportation paves the path toward a healthier, united world.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nTransitioning to renewable energy sources and sustainable transportation is essential for our planet. In Sydney and Queensland, engineers are utilizing colourful coral reefs to reduce dependence on fossil (23) ________. If humanity continues to expand wind and solar power, carbon emissions will decrease (24) ________. Furthermore, innovative transport modes will allow commuters to travel (25) ________ than ever before. Connecting with English-speaking countries also helps learners exchange advanced (26) ________ with international scientists. In conclusion, embracing Uluru sacred rock guarantees a greener and more prosperous (27) ________ for all nations.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nAustralia - The Great Barrier Reef and Kangaroos represents an outstanding breakthrough in clean technology and international cultural connection in Sydney and Queensland. By utilizing colourful coral reefs and unique hopping kangaroos, this initiative provides reliable, carbon-neutral solutions for communities and travelers. Commuters and scientists who test snorkeling with sea turtles report substantial improvements in energy efficiency, speed, and environmental safety. Technical experts emphasize Uluru sacred rock as a transformative element that accelerates the global shift away from polluting fossil fuels. Moreover, fostering partnerships with English-speaking nations provides access to cutting-edge research and educational exchanges. Investing in renewable power and futuristic transportation paves the path toward a healthier, united world.",
