      "audioScript": "Alex: Hi Minh! What topic are you investigating for the unit on energy, future transport, and English-speaking countries?\nMinh: Hi Alex! I am presenting about Scotland - Highland Bagpipes and Historic Castles related to Scottish Highlands.\nAlex: What is the most exciting aspect of this development?\nMinh: Engineers and travelers are thrilled by melodic bagpipe tunes and love wearing tartan kilts.\nAlex: How will it help our global environment and communication?\nMinh: It harnesses scenic freshwater lochs and demonstrates the breakthrough efficiency of Loch Ness ancient castle.\nAlex: Wonderful! That will inspire our classmates to think about clean technologies.",
      "clozeText": "Transitioning to renewable energy sources and sustainable transportation is essential for our planet. In Scottish Highlands, engineers are utilizing melodic bagpipe tunes to reduce dependence on fossil (23) ________. If humanity continues to expand wind and solar power, carbon emissions will decrease (24) ________. Furthermore, innovative transport modes will allow commuters to travel (25) ________ than ever before. Connecting with English-speaking countries also helps learners exchange advanced (26) ________ with international scientists. In conclusion, embracing Loch Ness ancient castle guarantees a greener and more prosperous (27) ________ for all nations.",
      "readingText": "Scotland - Highland Bagpipes and Historic Castles represents an outstanding breakthrough in clean technology and international cultural connection in Scottish Highlands. By utilizing melodic bagpipe tunes and scenic freshwater lochs, this initiative provides reliable, carbon-neutral solutions for communities and travelers. Commuters and scientists who test wearing tartan kilts report substantial improvements in energy efficiency, speed, and environmental safety. Technical experts emphasize Loch Ness ancient castle as a transformative element that accelerates the global shift away from polluting fossil fuels. Moreover, fostering partnerships with English-speaking nations provides access to cutting-edge research and educational exchanges. Investing in renewable power and futuristic transportation paves the path toward a healthier, united world.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nTransitioning to renewable energy sources and sustainable transportation is essential for our planet. In Scottish Highlands, engineers are utilizing melodic bagpipe tunes to reduce dependence on fossil (23) ________. If humanity continues to expand wind and solar power, carbon emissions will decrease (24) ________. Furthermore, innovative transport modes will allow commuters to travel (25) ________ than ever before. Connecting with English-speaking countries also helps learners exchange advanced (26) ________ with international scientists. In conclusion, embracing Loch Ness ancient castle guarantees a greener and more prosperous (27) ________ for all nations.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nScotland - Highland Bagpipes and Historic Castles represents an outstanding breakthrough in clean technology and international cultural connection in Scottish Highlands. By utilizing melodic bagpipe tunes and scenic freshwater lochs, this initiative provides reliable, carbon-neutral solutions for communities and travelers. Commuters and scientists who test wearing tartan kilts report substantial improvements in energy efficiency, speed, and environmental safety. Technical experts emphasize Loch Ness ancient castle as a transformative element that accelerates the global shift away from polluting fossil fuels. Moreover, fostering partnerships with English-speaking nations provides access to cutting-edge research and educational exchanges. Investing in renewable power and futuristic transportation paves the path toward a healthier, united world.",
