      "audioUrl": "/web-tieng-anh/audio/listening_9_ck2.mp3",
      "audioScript": "Ben: Hi Trang! What topic on space exploration, digital devices, or career orientation are you analyzing?\nTrang: Hi Ben! I am presenting about Electronic Waste (E-Waste) Recycling and Circular Electronics at electronics recycling facility.\nBen: What is the most inspiring aspect of this subject?\nTrang: Experts and students are captivated by recovering rare earth precious metals and eager to explore sorting circuit motherboard components.\nBen: How does it prepare ninth graders for future academic and professional success?\nTrang: It provides deep perspectives on safely dismantling old lithium batteries and underscores the significance of circular electronics engineer.\nBen: Fantastic! That provides actionable guidance for our class as we prepare for high school.",
      "clozeText": "Preparing for future careers, understanding digital devices, and exploring space are essential for ninth graders. In electronics recycling facility, researchers and career advisors utilize recovering rare earth precious metals to prepare students for the global (23) ________. If students actively engage in sorting circuit motherboard components, they will acquire adaptable vocational and digital (24) ________. Many educators emphasized that electronic gadgets (25) ________ utilized responsibly rather than for mindless distraction. Furthermore, advancing our understanding of safely dismantling old lithium batteries reminds us of our responsibility toward Earth and the wider (26) ________. In conclusion, cultivating circular electronics engineer will empower youth to navigate modern challenges and build a fulfilling (27) ________.",
      "readingText": "Electronic Waste (E-Waste) Recycling and Circular Electronics stands at the intersection of technological transformation, future vocational readiness, and cosmic curiosity in electronics recycling facility. As artificial intelligence and automated devices reshape employment landscapes, recovering rare earth precious metals and safely dismantling old lithium batteries offer invaluable career pathways. Students and professionals who commit to sorting circuit motherboard components report enhanced digital literacy, cognitive flexibility, and professional confidence. Industry mentors and career counselors highlight circular electronics engineer as an indispensable asset that bridges academic knowledge with commercial reality. Moreover, whether contemplating human settlements beyond Earth or mastering electronic communication, students broaden their ambitions. By combining technical proficiency, critical inquiry, and lifelong dedication, ninth graders will lead society toward extraordinary achievements.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nPreparing for future careers, understanding digital devices, and exploring space are essential for ninth graders. In electronics recycling facility, researchers and career advisors utilize recovering rare earth precious metals to prepare students for the global (23) ________. If students actively engage in sorting circuit motherboard components, they will acquire adaptable vocational and digital (24) ________. Many educators emphasized that electronic gadgets (25) ________ utilized responsibly rather than for mindless distraction. Furthermore, advancing our understanding of safely dismantling old lithium batteries reminds us of our responsibility toward Earth and the wider (26) ________. In conclusion, cultivating circular electronics engineer will empower youth to navigate modern challenges and build a fulfilling (27) ________.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nElectronic Waste (E-Waste) Recycling and Circular Electronics stands at the intersection of technological transformation, future vocational readiness, and cosmic curiosity in electronics recycling facility. As artificial intelligence and automated devices reshape employment landscapes, recovering rare earth precious metals and safely dismantling old lithium batteries offer invaluable career pathways. Students and professionals who commit to sorting circuit motherboard components report enhanced digital literacy, cognitive flexibility, and professional confidence. Industry mentors and career counselors highlight circular electronics engineer as an indispensable asset that bridges academic knowledge with commercial reality. Moreover, whether contemplating human settlements beyond Earth or mastering electronic communication, students broaden their ambitions. By combining technical proficiency, critical inquiry, and lifelong dedication, ninth graders will lead society toward extraordinary achievements.",
      "writingRubric": "Tiêu chí chấm điểm (1.0đ): Mention: Context in electronics recycling facility; Key factors like recovering rare earth precious metals; Recommended activities like sorting circuit motherboard components; Role of circular electronics engineer in future careers.",
